  - SeqCode
  - LPSN
  - prokaryotes
  - bioinformatics
abstract: >-
  prokname is a command-line tool and Python library for assisting
  researchers in naming new prokaryotic taxa (bacteria and archaea) under
  the International Code of Nomenclature of Prokaryotes (ICNP) and the
  SeqCode. It provides deterministic, rule-based generation of candidate
  names from etymology inputs, dual-mode genus gender determination,
  grammatical agreement validation (three-way categories: true adjective,
  genitive noun, appositive noun), dual-code routing (ICNP vs SeqCode with
  ICNP-preemption awareness), and two-tier deduplication (authority APIs +
  local parahomonym scan). The tool is designed for reproducibility and
  auditability: all rules are versioned JSON data assets, no large language
  models are used in the core pipeline, and every output carries source
  attribution and license information.
preferred-citation:
